# Fractal Slice Architecture (FSA)

**ADR:** [docs/adr/0007-fractal-slice-architecture.md](../../docs/adr/0007-fractal-slice-architecture.md)  
**Workflows:** [docs/conventions/fsa-workflows.md](../../docs/conventions/fsa-workflows.md)  
**Target detail (draft):** [docs/architecture/fractal-slice-architecture.md](../../docs/architecture/fractal-slice-architecture.md)

Load this rule when adding features, migrating a slug to FSA, touching cross-feature imports, or introducing integration hubs.

## Module shape (target)

Each registry slug under `src/features/<slug>/`:

```text
public-api/     → presentation.ts | infrastructure.ts | types.ts (segregated; no mixed barrel)
internal/       → presentation/ | core/ | infrastructure/ (private)
features/       → nested sub-slices (optional, same rules)
```

**Entry/orchestrator:** `src/app/`, `server.ts` — thin wiring only.  
**Shared UI:** `src/components/` — no feature `internal/` imports.

## Three rules (enforce on every change)

1. **Segregated contracts** — Import another feature only from `@/features/<slug>/public-api/presentation`, `…/infrastructure`, or `…/types`. Never a single mixed `index.ts` for presentation + server code.

2. **No cross-feature internal imports** — `src/features/<a>/internal/**` is private to `<a>`. Forbidden: `@/features/other/internal/...`.

3. **Deletion test** — Slice-specific code lives under `src/features/<slug>/` (plus `src/app` routes and registry). Do not add slice-only logic to global `src/hooks/` or anonymous shared utils without an owner.

## Next.js constraints (breaking if violated)

- **App Router only in `src/app/`** — `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `route.ts`, etc. Never move route files into `src/features/`.
- **API handlers** — thin `src/app/api/**/route.ts`; delegate to `public-api/infrastructure` or `src/lib/`.
- **Custom server** — root `server.ts` (ADR 0002); no WebSocket upgrade inside feature `internal/`.
- **Client boundary** — `'use client'` modules import only `public-api/presentation` and `public-api/types`. Never `public-api/infrastructure` or `internal/infrastructure/**`.
- **No new top-level roots** (e.g. `src/shared/`, `src/hubs/`) without `structure-validation.config.json` + ADR update in the same PR.
- **Verify migrations** — `npm run build` or harness `verify` workflow after any FSA code move.

## Cross-feature effects

- Prefer **integration hubs** under `src/hubs/<Name>/` (command/query split).
- Features may depend on hubs; hubs must not depend on feature `internal/`.
- Do not introduce domain-wide pub/sub for traceable business coupling.

## Agent playbooks (required)

| Task | Command |
| ---- | ------- |
| New capability | `@.cursor/commands/command-fsa-implement-feature.md` |
| Migrate one slug | `@.cursor/commands/command-fsa-migrate-feature.md` |
| Verify | `@.cursor/commands/command-verify-post-change-lint-typecheck-tests.md` |

Run `npm run harness:bootstrap -- --match="FSA"` to resolve workflow. One slug per migration unless the user batches.

## Coexistence with ADR 0003

`libPath` and flat `hooks/` / `utils/` are **legacy layout** until migrated. New code in an FSA-scaffolded slug goes under `internal/` and `public-api/`.

